A||||15||Robert||Beware …… they’re back…….||||12||
Z||000000||Robert||01-16-2001||07:31 PM||||I’m sitting in my computer room, working away at my tennis clubs web site <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net" TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net</A>  when I hear a soft knock at the door.  Being at an impasse of thought (in other words, stuck on what to write next) I answered the door.  <P>BIG MISTAKE!!!!!<P>There with the face of an angle is one of the local kids, in her Girl Scout uniform, selling the dreaded “Girl Scout Cookies”….<P>Yes, people, it’s that time of the year again.<BR>I don’t think I’ve lost the weight I gained from last year’s barrage.  <BR>What else could I do but buy several boxes of cookies, which will translate to 10 pounds of weight on me.<P>This is just a warning to all of you out there, they are on the move, you will see them in front of your favorite stores, walking up and down your streets and even your co-workers will be bringing in the order forms.  There is no escape….<P>Robert<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> <P> “If you don’t look for that parking space near the entrance, you’ll never get it”||||reg||12
Z||000001||Black88GT||01-16-2001||08:07 PM||||Last year to combat the girl scouts, I went all out warfare on them.  <P>For 2000, I put up 12 foot fences with razor sharp barbwire all around the perimeter of my house.  Those fences were electrified using a prison type system, only with a little more juice.  I then installed 150 anti-personnel land mines, 50 anti-tank mines, and my personal favorite, 20 remote activated Claymore mines around the walkways.  I built (4) 25 foot guard towers and hired a small army to guard the front gates, with cameras to monitor all activities of course.  I then used a Camp David type system of trip wires and motion detectors for 50 yards each way from the gates.  If there comin', I want some time to prepare.  <P>I thought that would be good enough.  Around 2100 hours on the night of January 13th, 2000 we had approx. 10 paratrooping girl scouts land beyond the gates, they managed to navigate through the mine field using adavnced mine detecting abilities.  However, we managed to take out 2 with Sniper fire from a guard tower, and little Suzy tripped up on a mine blowing the right side of her body into 3 pieces.  Still, 7 managed to reach the doorbell so I was trapped into buying 5 boxes.  <P>For 2001, I have added 8 50mm Anti-Aircraft cannons and 2 Surface-to-Air Missile silos with built in radar, russian designed.  I had considered purchasing some T-72 russian tanks but, I thought that might be a little overkill.  As a last line of defense, I installed an intricate doorbell system design.  3 different colored buttons, with a code you must match in order to activate the bell.  If the code is not matched, 2 "Bouncing Betty's" are activated from the rose gardens.  For security reasons, the code is change every 24 hours and automatically sent to my pager.<P>As of 1900 hours today we have no sign of them, we are prepared for anything they can throw at us....<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">               <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">               <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 01-16-2001).]||||reg||1
